{
  "id": "ep230",
  "duration": 58.09,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.456,
      "text": "A cosmic abyss two billion light-years wide is stealing light's energy.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Dark Flow (4423361836).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA Goddard Space Flight Center from Greenbelt, MD, USA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dark_Flow_(4423361836).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.456,
      "end": 12.201,
      "text": "Spanning nearly two billion light-years across, the Eridanus Supervoid holds the record as space's most massive emptiness.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Johann Bayer - Eridanus.jpg",
        "credit": "Johann Bayer",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johann_Bayer_-_Eridanus.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.467,
          "end": 7.667,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 7.667,
          "end": 12.2,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 12.201,
      "end": 19.446,
      "text": "Inside this titanic cosmic hole, vast amounts of galaxies, gas, and invisible dark matter are missing.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Cosmic Gems Within the Antlia Cluster (noirlab2501b).jpg",
        "credit": "Dark Energy Survey/DOE/FNAL/DECam/CTIO/NOIRLab/NSF/AURA Image processing: R. Colombari & M. Zamani (NSF NOIRLab)",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cosmic_Gems_Within_the_Antlia_Cluster_(noirlab2501b).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 12.2,
          "end": 15.8,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 15.8,
          "end": 19.433,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 19.446,
      "end": 28.166,
      "text": "When ancient light from 380,000 years after the Big Bang enters the void, dark energy accelerates space's expansion.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "CMB universe expansion.png",
        "credit": "NASA/WMAP Science Team/ Art by Dana Berry",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CMB_universe_expansion.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 19.433,
          "end": 28.167,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 28.166,
      "end": 34.686,
      "text": "The stretched gravitational landscape drains energy from passing photons, cooling them as they exit.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "WMAP 2012.png",
        "credit": "NASA / WMAP Science Team",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WMAP_2012.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 28.167,
          "end": 30.7,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 30.7,
          "end": 34.7,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 34.686,
      "end": 43.106,
      "text": "This creates a region roughly 70 microkelvin colder than the universe's average background temperature, wrapped in a warm ring.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Art Institute of Chicago (CC0)",
        "title": "Bowl Depicting Rows of Spotted Birds",
        "credit": "Nazca\nSouth coast, Peru",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://www.artic.edu/artworks/6404"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 34.7,
          "end": 38.9,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 38.9,
          "end": 43.1,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 43.106,
      "end": 51.206,
      "text": "Yet standard cosmological calculations reveal this void expansion can only explain a fraction of the deep chill.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "V\u00edctor M Blanco 4-meter Telescope (12-0329-12Dhr-CC).jpg",
        "credit": "DOE/FNAL/DECam/R. Hahn/CTIO/NOIRLab/NSF/AURA",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:V%C3%ADctor_M_Blanco_4-meter_Telescope_(12-0329-12Dhr-CC).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 43.1,
          "end": 48.133,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 48.133,
          "end": 51.2,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 51.206,
      "end": 57.74,
      "text": "No known physical process should drain energy from the Big Bang's relic radiation so aggressively.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Dark Flow (4423361836).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA Goddard Space Flight Center from Greenbelt, MD, USA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dark_Flow_(4423361836).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 51.2,
          "end": 58.1,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
